{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]He came to Jesus by night
Asked [Gm]how a man can [Dm]be born [Eb]new
No signs like yours without [Gm]God
But how can this be done [Dm]for you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Un[Eb]less someone is born of water and the Spirit
[Gm]He cannot enter [Dm]the kingdom of God
What [Eb]is born of the flesh is flesh
[Gm]And what is born of the Spirit is spir[Eb]it
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I told you truly and again
[Gm]You must be born [Dm]from a[Eb]bove
Do not be astonished at this [Gm]word
The wind blows where it wills, [Dm]no love lost
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Un[Eb]less someone is born of water and the Spirit
[Gm]He cannot enter [Dm]the kingdom of God
What [Eb]is born of the flesh is flesh
[Cm]And what is born of the Spir[Gm]it is spir[Bb]it
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
You hear its sound but [F]not [Cm]its source
Where it comes from [Gm]or goes, unknown
So [Eb]it is with every[F]one
Born of the Spirit, [Gm]standing alone
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Unless some[Dm]one is born of [Eb]water and the Spirit
He cannot enter the [Gm]kingdom of God
What [Dm]is born of the flesh is [Eb]flesh
And what is born of the [Gm]Spirit is spirit
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
How can [Dm]this be, I ask
[Eb]Born of water and the Spir[Gm]it
{end_of_verse}

